    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d937">

                <pb facs="0728" n="612" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg612"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/13581.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Special Agent Canova to
                        the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Aguascalientes</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-10-23T23:00:00-06:36">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">October 23, 1914, 11 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Replying to Convention’s telegram beseeching him to submit his resignation,
                    Carranza answers he will not do so; that he will deliver the Executive Power
                    only to the president who shall have been elected by the people.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Canova</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
